From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:02:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] docs: correct the 1.0.0 capability claims the code does
 not back

The 1.0.0 CHANGELOG, the v1.0 release notes and the README feature
overview list capabilities that were never delivered in 1.0.x: a gRPC
transport to the Node Agent, an end-to-end execution plane test,
network partition and GPU fault injection chaos tests, Prometheus and
OpenTelemetry export, process-level plugin isolation, enforced
manifest signature checks and a production Temporal integration.
Three more (no 501 endpoints, mandatory authentication, SSRF
allowlist) only became true in 1.1.0.

Keep the historical entries and add errata instead, as the 1.0.1 notes
did for the PostgreSQL claim. Annotate each README overview item with
its current state and refresh the test statistics.
